      "investigation": "PSI-26",
      "acronym": "BASS",
      "about": null,
      "kind": "NASA document",
      "evidence_level": "moderate",
      "file": "PSI-26_Presentations_Flammability Aspects of Fabric_USNationalCombustion2013.pdf",
      "page": 35,
      "text": "Summary\n\n♦ For the opposed flow configuration, the flame quickly reached steady\nspread for each flow speed, and the spread rate was fastest at an\nintermediate value of flow speed.\n\n♦ These tests show the enhanced flammability in microgravity for this\ngeometry, since, in normal gravity air, a flame self-extinguishes in\nthe opposed flow geometry (downward flame spread).",
      "cites": [
       "PSI-26"
      ],
      "doi": "10.60555/58h4-dy80"
