      "text": "There are 3 fuel nozzles made for the SPICE experiment. They all have the same length; 50 mm,\nwith different inner diameters: 0.41 mm, 0.76 mm and 1.6 mm, respectively. Only one of the three\nnozzles is installed during a burn. Figure 4 is a photo of the igniters and nozzles in a storage box\nshipped to ISS. It can be seen that a nozzle has two parts: a thicker base with female threads in it and\na piece of thin tubing extended from the base. Thus the nozzle is threaded on a connector inside the\nflow duct, on the left hand side in Fig. 3. After installation, the nozzle is along the center line of flow\nduct. Its tip is about 54 mm from the screen at the left end of the flow duct.",
