      "page": 8,
      "text": "Ambient Oxygen Concentration Requirements\nn/a\nOn each day of testing, the oxygen\nconcentration of the ISS cabin atmosphere\nshould be measured. Testing is\nrestricted to oxygen concentrations at\nor above 21% O2.\nn/a\nWhen possible, the oxygen concentration\nwithin the MSG working volume shall be\nknown during testing. It should be\npossible for a crewmember to measure the\noxygen concentration within the MSG\nworking volume with a CSA-CP\n(Compound Specific Analyzer –\nCombustion Products). Testing is\nrestricted to oxygen concentrations at\nor above 21% O2.\nn/a\nThe oxygen concentration can be\nmeasured by the MCA (Major Constituent\nAnalyzer) or oxygen sensors in the\nColumbus module or Service Module (i.e.,\nZarya). The oxygen concentration could\nalso be measured by a crewmember using\na CSA-CP (Compound Specific Analyzer –\nCombustion Products). If possible, it is\ndesired that the same O2 measurement\nsensor be used for all tests to eliminate\nvariation between instruments.",
