      "text": "Test day 20190 is a makeup of 20155, with 45% H2 / 55% He issuing into 30% O2 / 70% He and\n21% O2 / 79% He. For both oxygen concentration environments, flow rates resulting in expanding\nflames lasted for a while but were cut off by automated protocol for burner temperature limit\nbefore radiative extinction. As for cases where the flow rates are ramped down, extinction\ndetection is observed for both oxygen concentration environments. It is not clear if extinction is\nkinetic or from heat loss to the burner. Detailed analyses are needed. Tests with a reduced\noxygen concentration atmosphere of 17.5% O2 / 82.5% He seems to show both radiative and\nkinetic extinction. Additional analyses are needed.\n\nD. Surprises and New Discoveries\nMany discoveries are expected to arise as the data is analyzed and computational simulations are\ncompared. Initial surprises and discoveries include:",
